    "q-162195": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162195",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u-2v-3,\\,y=u-v+2.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?",
      "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-2v-3 \\\\ u-v+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-2v \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-2)=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|0|=0.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
